GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "89B833D6A0FBFD15"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{37F54398CF0FDBDE}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "HitTheMan's Domination"
     m_sContent "<h2>Domination</h2>"\
     "<b>Welcome!</b>"\
     "This is my very barebone recreation of Domination from ArmA 2/3 days by utilizing TILW's Framework as I am not a script kiddie unfortunately."\
     ""\
     "So what is Domination? At it's essence its a gamemode where objectives will pop up where the team work together to clear them before proceeding to the next, with potential rewards like vehicles, acces to weapons, etc."\
     ""\
     "I am hoping to slowly work on this and recreate that experience, and I hope people playing will try to work together and do teamwork and coordination like we do during our usual game sessions during the weekends."\
     ""\
     ""\
     ""\
     "TLDR:"\
     "A gamemode where we can enjoy coordination and teamwork while completing tasks & objectives, during the weekday or hours before the session starts."\
     ""\
     "Read Features for more details."
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D4586733A3811546}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "A. Enemy Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces:</h2>"\
     "<b>Equipment:</b>"\
     "USSR are equipped with their standard WARSAW Pact weaponry, AK series, RPG7s, RPKs."\
     "Wearing the standard USSR uniform of Tan Camo with greenish helmet."\
     ""\
     "<b>Known Strength:</b>"\
     "1x  BMP-1 Company (-)"\
     ""\
     "<b>Location: </b>"\
     "Located East of our position (Marked on map)"\
     ""\
     "<b>Capabilities:</b>"\
     "Access to RPKs, RPGs."\
     "Vehicles include BMP-1s"\
     ""\
     "<b>MLCOA:</b>"\
     "Push up toward the bridge, dismount 300m from it before conducting the assault"\
     ""\
     "<b>MDCOA:</b>"\
     "Push up toward the bridge, dismount 300m from it before commencing a BMP Bombardment before conducting their assault"\
     ""\
     "<b>Defensive Fires:</b>"\
     "No known threat at this time."\
     ""\
     "<b>Airthreat:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>Morale:</b>"\
     "VERY High."\
     ""\
     "<b>CBRN Threat:</b>"\
     "The enemy pose no CBRN Threat."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{06CD14F99FD50205}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "B. Friendly Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>B. Friendly Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>a. Disposition:</b>"\
     "Our Battalion is located to the S-W, we're spread out fairly wide to be able to locate any potential hostile movement while also maintaining security."\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Higher Units Mission:</b>"\
     "Battalion has been tasked with locating any potential soviet build up before consolidating into a defensive line."\
     ""\
     "A few hours prior we engaged and killed 2x BRDMs & 1x BMP-1 who were likely conducting recon, thankfully nothing major and were easy to deal with as lured them in close before engaging."\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Composition:</b>"\
     "1x Platoon (-)"\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Strength:</b>"\
     "1st Platoon - At 26 Man Strength"\
     ""\
     "<b>e. Supporting Fires:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>f. Attachments/Detachments:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>g. Additional Ammunition</b>"\
     "None."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CA6E76FEC54BE981}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "II. Mission (Must Read):"
     m_sContent "<h2>II: Mission</h2>"\
     "Prevent the loss of our forward positions that is the Bridge at 060 069 & Campsite at 055 068 as marked on map."\
     ""\
     "We have 1000x Sandbags + 10x Backpacks in a crate near us to be able to set up our forward positions."\
     ""\
     "Be wary of the BMP-1's HEFRAG rounds"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3345C1E5D745E941}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "II. Features:"
     m_sContent "<h2>II: A. Features</h2>"\
     "<b>Command Truck:</b>"\
     "There is a Command Truck next to HQ that can act as a Forward Spawn Point, where you can Teleport to it from the HQ Flag."\
     ""\
     "Be mindful you can TP while its moving, and that it takes 5min to respawn should it be destroyed. Which means you'll either have to drive or utilize the Mi-8s"\
     ""\
     "<b>Set Weather/Time in-game:</b>"\
     "Players can set Weather/Time in-game at the HQ by looking at the Flipcharts, to change the gameplay & experience."\
     ""\
     "<b>\"Random Objectives\":</b>"\
     "A bit false as its not truly random (Cannot figure it out) but more objectives will be added and made to function at a random sequence"\
     ""\
     "<b>Command Trucks:</b>"\
     "There is a Command Truck next to HQ that can act as a Forward Spawn Point, where you can Teleport to it from the HQ Flag."\
     ""\
     "Be mindful you can TP while its moving, and that it takes 5min to respawn should it be destroyed. Which means you'll either have to drive or utilize the Mi-8s"\
     ""\
     "<b>Respawns:</b>"\
     "There is about 1,000,000 respawn tickets, this may change where you gain tickets from completing objectives BUT for now you'll instantly respawn, along with vehicles at their cooldown."\
     ""\
     "<b>Hostile QRF:</b>"\
     "Should you get near the Antenna and the enemy spots you, they will call in QRF to reinforce the objective. This can be Infantry, APC, IFV or even Tanks. "\
     ""\
     "Destroying the Antenna will deny them the reinforcements."\
     ""\
     "<b>AI Inside Buildings:</b>"\
     "AI will be spawned inside buildings occupying them. NOT all buildings as we'd have far too many AI for the server to handle, but there will be AI in some if not most buildings depending on the location the objective spawns."\
     ""\
     "<b>Supply System:</b>"\
     "There is now a Supply System in place where you can purchase new vehicles, equipment, ammo and more. Use it sparingly as the only way to get more supply is by completing Main Objectives, and also scavenge/steal any supplies might be located there back to our HQ"\
     ""\
     "<b>Side Objectives:</b>"\
     "A Side objective that's smaller but can potentially reward in newer vehicles like Tanks, Mi-24s, etc."\
     ""\
     "<b>Rewards:</b>"\
     "Main Objectives now gives rewards for completing them, sometimes access to new vehicles and equipment, but will always provide an amount of supplies to the HQ's stockpile for us to utilize for future missions."\
     "There is also supplies in the objective themselves that can be scavenged/stolen by loading up a truck or Mi-8 (or any vehicle capable of carrying supplies) and bring it back to Main HQ Supply Depot"\
     ""\
     "Side Objectives now also give free vehicles as well as supplies"\
     ""\
     "<b>Activate Missions:</b>"\
     "You can activate the next sequence of Main OR Side Objectives at will at HQ, to minimize amount of AI to make Side Objectives more challenging or to prepare before the Separatists move in."\
     ""\
     "<h2>II: B. Planned Features</h2>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Ambushes:</b>"\
     "Sometimes while driving down the road you may get ambushed by infantry or perhaps even vehicles, I know of a easy way to do this."\
     ""\
     "<b>More Objectives and perhaps a varied variety:</b>"\
     "I got ideas for a more variety of objectives than a simple \"Clear Town + Destroy Antenna\", which can be easily added to the pool."\
     ""\
     "<b>Indirect Fire:</b>"\
     "Give AI indirect fire support, be it via triggers or a mortar team (if I can figure out AI mortar firing system)"\
     ""\
     "<b>COTVT Variant or even TVT Variant:</b>"\
     "Have either a very small 4-5 man strong defender team that can teleport to objectives to stay inside them to give more challenge to the players"\
     "OR have two competing teams to clear objectives first, maybe giving the succeeding team with new better vehicles."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Open for Suggestions or Improvements</h2>"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{07B497A9854DB774}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "III. Features:"
     m_sContent "<h2>III. Mission</h2>"\
     "<b>Main Objectives:</b>"\
     ""\
     "Main Objectives are large towns that gets overrun by Seperatists, who fortify the place and bring in supplies and heavy equipment."\
     ""\
     "Side Objectives are more specalized tasks to hit the enemy where it hurts while gaining free vehicles as rewards and supplies."\
     ""\
     "Our objective is to recapture and drive out the Seperatists from these towns or critical locations."\
     ""\
     "We can also take any supplies they have there to bring back to our HQ to allow High Command to supply us with more and better vehicles (They are marked on map)"\
     ""\
     "As we capture them we also unlock new vehicles and equipment as well."
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CCE431C91BF90D2E}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "III. Execution:"
     m_sContent "<h2>III: Execution</h2>"\
     "<b>Intent:</b>"\
     "Protect our Battalion Flank and ensuring we do not lose our positions."\
     ""\
     "<b>1. Concept of the Operation:</b>"\
     "Platoon Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is advised to utilize our sandbags to setup forward and fallback positions."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Maneuver</b>"\
     "Platoon Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is advised to not split up the squads too much or too far ahead so they can mutually support one another if needed."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{86EE14EAB4E816AA}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "IV. Sustainment:"
     m_sContent "<h2>IV: Sustainment</h2>"\
     "<b>a. SOP Variations</b>"\
     "Dress: Standard Canadian Uniform"\
     "Equipment: Standard Canadian Loadout"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Logistical Support:</b>"\
     "Replen Plan: None for 24h."\
     "Ammunition: Each man carries his own ammunition."\
     "IPE: Helmets and body armour are to be worn at all times."\
     ""\
     "Crate outside contains:"\
     "- 1000x Sandbags"\
     "- 10x Backpacks"\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Medical:</b>"\
     "Location: Company Aid Post is to be setup by platoon medic."\
     "CASEVAC: By foot or with Platoon Assets like HMMWVs if there are any."\
     "Plan: Set up a casualty collection point and extract casualties to this point."\
     "Stretchers: None"\
     "Med Packs: Platoon medpack carried by platoon medic."\
     "Morphine: Every soldier carries 1+ stick of morphine."\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Vehicles:</b>"\
     "None."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{11E65A343D3DAA0D}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "IV. Enemy Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces:</h2>"\
     "<b>Equipment:</b>"\
     "Seperatists are equipped with their a variety of weaponry but mostly consisting of WARSAW Pact weaponry."\
     "Wearing a Mix match of coloured camo uniforms & helmets."\
     ""\
     "<b>Capabilities:</b>"\
     "Access to M113s, BRDMs, BMP-1s, T-72As, RPGs, PKMs, etc."\
     ""\
     "<b>Defensive Fires:</b>"\
     "No known threat at this time."\
     ""\
     "<b>Airthreat:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>Morale:</b>"\
     "Incredibly High."\
     ""\
     "<b>CBRN Threat:</b>"\
     "The enemy pose no CBRN Threat... That we know of."
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F10F639E2AB234F1}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "V. Command & Signals:"
     m_sContent "<b>I. Chain of Command:</b>"\
     "21, 21 Alpha, 21 Bravo"\
     ""\
     "<b>II. Callsigns:</b>"\
     "Platoon HQ ------------------ 21"\
     "1st Section ------------------- 21A - Alpha"\
     "2nd Section ------------------ 21B - Bravo"\
     "3rd Section ------------------- 21C - Charlie"\
     ""\
     "<b>III. Frequencies:</b>"\
     "1st Platoon Net ------------ 48.00 MHz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{BB4F74D558733CA4}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "V. Logistics & Support:"
     m_sContent "<h2>IV: Logistics & Support.</h2>"\
     "<b>a. Vehicle Respawns.</b>"\
     "Only Engineering Group's Vehicles (Engineer, Repair, Fuel) and Transport (UAZ, Urals, Ambulances) will respawn 5min after being destroyed (Burned up and exploded)"\
     ""\
     "Otherwise all other vehicles are finite and costs resources, which can be aquired from completing main objectives or scavanging from them."\
     ""\
     "There are Repair & Refuel trucks that the engineers (or anyone) can use to try and recover vehicles, refuel them among other things."\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Logistical Support:</b>"\
     "Vehicle Service is marked on map where you can repair and refuel your vehicles. "\
     "An arsenal is near HQ that can be utilized to aquire more ammunition or equipment as needed."\
     ""\
     "A Engineer Truck can be used to establish FOBs, Checkpoints, Mortar Pits or simple fortifications as needed."\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Medical:</b>"\
     "There are 2x Ambulance UAZs that the medics (or anyone) can utilize to heal wounds in the field, using the ambulance mechanic to heal broken limbs or fill with supplies to spawn more medical equipment as needed."\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Vehicles:</b>"\
     "2x BRDM-2s"\
     "1x Command Ural (You can TP to it from the HQ)"\
     "2x Engineer Urals"\
     "2x Repair Urals"\
     "2x Fuel Urals"\
     "3x Ural Transports"\
     "3x UAZ 452 Transports"\
     "3x UAZs"\
     "2x UAZ452 Ambulances"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C456552B9537563E}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "VI. Command & Signals:"
     m_sContent "<b>I. Chain of Command:</b>"\
     "340 -> 341 HQ -> 344 HQ -> 347 (HQ) -> 341 -> etc"\
     ""\
     "<b>II. Callsigns:</b>"\
     "Company HQ ------------------------------ 340 (Radio)"\
     "Forward Air Support Liasons ------------ KAMENKA"\
     "Engineer Group --------------------------- 355"\
     ""\
     "1st Platoon HQ --------------------------- 341 (HQ)"\
     "1st Rifle Squad --------------------------- 341"\
     "2nd Rifle Squad -------------------------- 342"\
     "3rd Rifle Squad --------------------------- 343"\
     ""\
     "2nd Platoon HQ -------------------------- 344 (HQ)"\
     "1st Rifle Squad --------------------------- 344"\
     "2nd Rifle Squad -------------------------- 345"\
     "3rd Rifle Squad --------------------------- 346"\
     ""\
     "1st Vehicle Crew --------------------------- 361v"\
     "2nd Vehicle Crew --------------------------- 362v"\
     ""\
     "1st Helicopter Pilot --------------------------- STAVOK 1"\
     "2nd Helicopter Pilot --------------------------- STAVOK 2"\
     ""\
     "- - - Vehicle Callsigns when Infantry dismounted:"\
     "340v - Victor"\
     "341v - Victor"\
     "342v - Victor"\
     "Etc."\
     ""\
     "<b>III. Frequencies:</b>"\
     "Company Net ------------------------------ 42.00 MHz"\
     "(YOU'RE ALL IN ONE NET, RADIO DISCIPLINE.)"\
     "Air Net -------------------------------------- 41.00 MHz"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{B0AA3561F206E8AF}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "VII. Air Control Manual (FASL MUST READ)"
     m_sContent "<h2>Table of Contents:</h2>"\
     "<b>- Different Types</b>"\
     "<b>- Example Transmissions between JTAC & Aircraft pilots:</b>"\
     "<b>- Formats for Transmissions</b> "\
     "<b>- Legends / Brevity Codes</b> "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>1) Type 1 Control.</h2>"\
     "<b>Type 1 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC must visually acquire the attacking Aircraft and the Mark / Target for control of each individual attack prior to weapons release / launch."\
     ""\
     "<h2>(2) Type 2 Control.</h2>"\
     "<b>Type 2 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC must visually acquire the attacking Aircraft OR the Mark / Target for control of each individual attack prior to weapons release / launch."\
     ""\
     "<h2>(3) Type 3 Control.</h2>"\
     "<b>Type 3 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC requires the ability to provide clearance for multiple attacks within a single engagement subject to specific attack restrictions. Type 3 control does not require the JTAC to visually acquire the aircraft or the target"\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Example 5-Line Brief Transmission:</h2> "\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31, Broadsword 11, 5-line, Type 2 control, BOT, rockets and guns, my position is checkpoint 295 marked by IR strobe, northwest 200, single technical vehicle marked by IR SPARKLE, make all attacks over my right shoulder, left pull, keep all effects of fires west of MSR Clovis.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Broadsword 11 (A/C):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31 copies over your right shoulder, left pull, keep all effects of fires west of MSR Clovis, pushing.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31, CONTINUE.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Broadsword 11 (A/C):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31 and flight, VISUAL, TALLY, IN.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31 and flight, CLEARED HOT.”<"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Example Situation Update Transmission:</h2> "\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31, Broadsword 11, Friendlies are two companies in the vicinity of OP 2, one on the high ground and the other in a blocking position to the east. I am with the company on the high ground. There is also a Recon team at the northwest tip of Black Mountain, arty is firecapped at Firebase 5E, firing generally west, Break.”"\
     ""\
     "“Current surface-to-air threat is a SA-6 at KJ 123 456, just west of MSR Tampa; target is light armored company attempting to flank us to the north and two companies dug in three klicks to our west, Over.”"\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Format: Rotary-Wing Close Air Support 5-Line Brief</h2> "\
     "Do not transmit line numbers. Units of measure are standard unless briefed. Restrictions are mandatory readback (*). JTAC may request additional readback. "\
     ""\
     "- 1. Observer/Warning Order"\
     "“(Aircraft Call Sign) _____________ , "\
     "This Is (JTAC Call Sign) _____________ , Over\" "\
     "5-line, Type (1, 2, or 3) C, MOA (BOC or BOT), (Ordnance Requested)"\
     ""\
     "- 2. Friendly Location/Mark "\
     "\"My position_____________ (TRP, Grid, etc.) , "\
     "Marked by _____________ (VS-17, Beacon, IR Strobe, etc.)\""\
     ""\
     "- 3. Target location "\
     "\"Target location, _________________________\" "\
     "(Bearing [magnetic] and Range [meters], TRP, Grid, etc.) "\
     ""\
     "- 4. Target Description/Mark"\
     "\" _____________ (Target Description) ,"\
     "marked by _____________ (IR sparkle, Tracer, etc.)\""\
     ""\
     "- 5. Remarks/Restrictions "\
     "*Final Attack Headings (FAHs) LTL/PTL "\
     "Surface-to-air threat"\
     "*Danger Close and initials"\
     "Additional calls requested"\
     "Additional remarks (GTL, weather, hazards, friendly mark)"\
     "*TOT/TTT "\
     ""\
     "The RW CAS 5-line should be passed as one transmission. If the restrictions portion is lengthy, it may be a separate transmission. "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Format: Situation Update (Controller to Close Air Support Aircraft)</h2>"\
     "<b>Situation Update # ____________________________ (if applicable) </b>"\
     "- Friendly Situation (disposition / posture, locations)"\
     "- Threat Activity (surface-to-air threats observed: who, what, when, where)"\
     "- Target – General Enemy Situation (“SALUTE” format – size, activity, location, uniform, time, equipment)"\
     "- Clearance Authority (Who has final control?)"\
     "- Ordnance Requested"\
     "- Restrictions"\
     "- Hazards (weather, terrain, obstructions)"\
     "- Remarks (JTAC capabilities, to include TLE if appropriate)"\
     ""\
     "Note: - This briefing should be broad in scope and will not be used as a substitute for a 5-line"\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Legends / Brevity Codes</h2>"\
     "<b>- VISUAL</b> = Sighting of a friendly aircraft/ground position. Opposite of BLIND."\
     ""\
     "<b>- BLIND</b> = No visual contact of friendly aircraft/ground position. Opposite of VISUAL."\
     ""\
     "<b>- NO JOY</b> = Aircrew does not have visual contact with the target / bandit / landmark. Opposite of TALLY."\
     ""\
     "<b>- TALLY</b> = Sighting of a target, non-friendly aircraft, landmark, or enemy position. Opposite of NO JOY."\
     ""\
     "<b>- BOT</b> = Bomb On Target"\
     ""\
     "<b>- TOT</b> = Time On Target"\
     ""\
     "<b>- TTT</b> = Time To Target"\
     ""\
     "<b>- SEAD</b> = Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses"\
     ""\
     "<b>- ABORT</b>= Directive call to cease action/attack/event/mission. Do not release ordnance."\
     ""\
     "<b>- CLEARED HOT</b>=  Ordnance release is authorized in Type 1 or 2 terminal attack controls. "\
     ""\
     "<b>- CLEARED TO ENGAGE</b>=  JTAC Type 3 control clearance. Attack aircraft flight leaders may initiate attacks within the parameters imposed by the JTAC. Attack platforms will provide a “Commencing Engagement” call prior to engaging targets and an “Engagement Complete” call to JTAC, indicating completion of ordnance release."\
     ""\
     "<b>- CONTINUE</b>=  Continue present maneuver. Does not imply a change in clearance to engage or expend ordnance."\
     ""\
     "<b>- CONTINUE DRY</b>=  Continue present maneuver, ordnance release not authorized. Used to provide approval to aircraft to continue the pass without expending ordnance during Type 1, 2, or 3* controls. (*JTAC must use “Type 3, Continue Dry” for dry Type 3 controls.)"\
     ""\
     "Note: - This briefing should be broad in scope and will not be used as a substitute for a 5-line"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CBC9B23190008E9F}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "Game Mastering Notes"
     m_sContent "<h2>Game Mastering</h2>"\
     "This mission is NOT designed for game mastering, should only be manipulated for technical, administrative or diagnostic purposes."
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
